{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfunzt2j7ebB1KjLcrEW5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The test function returns before the assertion settles, so in a naive runner the test could pass even if the promise resolves to something other than `1` or rejects. Any failure would surface later as an unhandled rejection, or not at all.\n\nRecent Vitest versions (2.1+) guard against this. They track unawaited `.resolves`/`.rejects` assertions, auto-await them when the test ends so failures are still reported, and print a warning like *\"Promise returned by `expect(actual).resolves.toBe(expected)` was not awaited… Please remember to await the assertion.\"* That warning also said a future major version would make this a hard failure, so check the behavior in your installed version.\n\nEither way, write `await expect(promise).resolves.toBe(1)` or `return` it. The `@vitest/eslint-plugin` rule `valid-expect` can catch the missing `await`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2251,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2251},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aa63684b-2140-41b7-b675-460e540b88a4","uuid":"922fb050-e22a-48f8-bf07-89a9f437bfd8","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:09:38.368Z","request_id":"req_011Cfunzsid2bXwW8vvz94pN"}
